{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And this is Ana.</b> The vav has the force of a weak peh, in the Ishmaelite language; in [the language of] RH it does not." "<b>The yemim.</b> Like \"the emim formerly\" (Deuteronomy 2:10), for alef is found interchanged with yod, like יתימרו. The Gaon [Saadia] says they are mules, and he explained \"found\" as \"he discovered the mounting.\" It is also possible that \"found\" means he was the first to discover this craft, for one species with another species does not produce offspring. This interpretation is strengthened by what the verse says: \"in his pasturing the donkeys.\" And if the yemim were plants, as many explain, what reason would there be to mention the donkeys?"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "RH likely = רבי חייא / רב הונא; abbreviation resolved with uncertainty.", 1 "'The mounting' (הרכיב) possibly refers to the act of crossbreeding; translated hyper-literally to preserve Ibn Ezra's compressed syntax."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:10.553328302Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}